Rips_Refund
├── when the rip does not exist
│   └── it should revert.
├── when recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert.
├── when the rip is not expired
│   ├── when the rip is not sold out but has not passed its duration
│   │   └── it should revert with {RipNotExpired}.
│   └── when the rip is sold out and the VRF request has not expired
│       └── it should revert with {RipNotExpired}.
├── when the recipient has already been refunded
│   └── it should revert.
├── when the recipient has no entries in the rip
│   └── it should revert.
├── given the stake currency is native
│   └── when the recipient has entries in the rip
│       ├── it should mark the recipient as refunded.
│       ├── it should transfer the ETH refund amount to the recipient.
│       ├── when recipient is different from the caller
│       │   └── it should transfer the ETH refund to the recipient, not the caller.
│       └── it should emit a {RefundIssued} event.
└── given the stake currency is an ERC20 token
    └── when the recipient has entries in the rip
        ├── it should mark the recipient as refunded.
        ├── it should transfer the token refund amount to the recipient.
        ├── when recipient is different from the caller
        │   └── it should transfer the token refund to the recipient, not the caller.
        └── it should emit a {RefundIssued} event.
